# File contexts for tafLegacyCApp.
#
# This is a bare native binary that is NOT packaged as a Legato app, so it does
# not live under /legato.  On this platform the rootfs is read-only, there is no
# /opt, /data and /tmp do not allow the SELinux domain transition (/data is
# noexec; /tmp is nosuid which blocks the bounded transition), so the binary is
# run from /var/volatile -- the only writable mount that is neither noexec nor
# nosuid.
#
# Notes for /var/volatile (tmpfs):
#  - It supports xattrs, so `restorecon -v /var/volatile/tafLegacyCApp` applies
#    this label and lets the shell->app domain transition (tafLegacyCApp.te)
#    fire.  Being neither noexec nor nosuid, the transition is not blocked.
#  - The label is NOT persistent: /var/volatile is cleared on reboot, so
#    re-copy and re-run restorecon after every boot.
#  - The policy module must already be loaded in the image for the
#    telaf_tafLegacyCApp_exec_t type to exist; otherwise restorecon falls back
#    to the mount's default label (var_t) and no transition can occur.

/var/volatile/tafLegacyCApp    --    gen_context(system_u:object_r:telaf_tafLegacyCApp_exec_t,s0)
